        ! THE BENCHMARK'S REALISED VALUES, NOT AN OLD ECONOMY'S.
        !
        ! A counterfactual overwrites both of these in upload_vars, from
        ! model_average_labour_income and median_income of the benchmark it
        ! imports (33621 and 33591). The BENCHMARK never calls upload_vars, so in
        ! the benchmark these declarations stand -- and they were written down
        ! from a finished run of an older economy. average_labor_income_calibrated
        ! read 0.637248 against the benchmark's realised 0.646389, and
        ! median_income_calibrated read 0.475981 against a realised 0.431324, ten
        ! per cent out.
        !
        ! The median one is inert: every voucher eligibility site selects
        ! is_counterfactual*median_income_calibrated and the benchmark takes
        ! median_income(time_period) instead. The income one is NOT inert -- the
        ! wealth and income histogram bin edges at 10605, 10619 and 10652 read it
        ! with no is_counterfactual selector, on the stated ground that a fixed
        ! constant "keeps the bin edges the same across points, which is what
        ! makes the shares comparable between vertices at all". That argument is
        ! right and the constant defeated it: the benchmark binned on 0.637248
        ! while every counterfactual binned on 0.646389, so the one comparison
        ! the bins exist to support was the one they did not hold for.
        !
        ! Both now carry the benchmark of record's realised values, so the two
        ! paths agree. check_benchmark_constants below warns if the benchmark
        ! moves away from them, because a constant written down from a finished
        ! run goes stale silently and this one did.
        ! UPDATED 9 SEPTEMBER to the CONVERGED benchmark's values, after the
        ! STALE CONSTANT guard below caught them one run after it was written:
        !
        !   average_labor_income_calibrated 0.64638853 -> realised 0.66786175
        !   median_income_calibrated        0.43132374 -> realised 0.37578380
        !
        ! Converging the equilibrium moved average labour income 3.3 per cent and
        ! the MEDIAN thirteen. The median is not cosmetic: voucher eligibility is
        ! threshold_income_vouchers*median_income_calibrated, so the cutoff moves
        ! 0.21566 to 0.18789 and the set of households a voucher can reach is
        ! thirteen per cent narrower. Every counterfactual reads this.
        real(8) :: average_labor_income_calibrated=&
            (1-perceived_probability_lower)*0.66786175+perceived_probability_lower*0.66786175
        ! STALE A THIRD TIME, CAUGHT 9 SEPTEMBER 19:00 BY THE GUARD BELOW.
        ! 0.37578380 was written down this morning from the converged benchmark
        ! and was out again by the afternoon. Four benchmark saves today, across
        ! two source revisions and both -O3 and -O1 -fcheck=bounds, realise the
        ! median at 0.38750440, 0.38750519, 0.38750373 and 0.38750473 -- six
        ! figures of agreement, so this is drift in the CONSTANT, not noise in
        ! the model.
        !
        ! WHAT IT COST. Voucher eligibility is threshold_income_vouchers times
        ! is_counterfactual*median_income_calibrated at six sites, and the
        ! benchmark takes median_income(time_period) instead. So the benchmark
        ! cut at 0.193752 and every counterfactual cut at 0.187892: the eligible
        ! set in the arms was 3.02 per cent narrower than the benchmark's own
        ! definition, and coverage is the channel the arms differ on.
        !
        ! THIS WILL GO STALE AGAIN at the next benchmark, and the guard is the
        ! only thing standing between that and another round of quietly wrong
        ! coverage. The durable fix is to write the realised median at save time
        ! and read it on the counterfactual path, the way drug_supply_shifter
        ! already works; that is a mechanism change and is the author's to take.
        real(8) :: median_income_calibrated=&
            (1-perceived_probability_lower)*0.38750473+perceived_probability_lower*0.38750473
        ! ZEROED BECAUSE THE GRID IT WAS TAKEN ON NO LONGER EXISTS.
        !
        ! These were average labour income at each of NINE evenly spaced nodes,
